      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good start. can u go a bit deeper on the nigerian and japanese segments? i'm worried about being too \"safe\" with the design. like, for nigeria, is there a specific way to design for them that doesn't feel too \"basic\" or \"charity-focused\"? sometimes fintech apps get too patronizing with emerging markets. also, for japan, you said minimal/traditional—does that mean we should avoid being too \"cutting edge\" or high-tech looking there to make sure they trust it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
