      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For Nigeria, avoid generic \"charity vibes\" by focusing on hyper-local relevance like mobile money authorization flows, clear Tiered Mobile Network operators (TMO) recognition, and vibrant but professional UI that signals financial liberation rather than aid. Keep the design confident and empowering, using bold yeres (colors) to stand out against a sea of competing apps without resorting to \"basics,\" ensuring Nigerians feel they are joining a serious global fintech partner.\n\nRegarding Japan, \"minimal\" doesn't mean avoiding a high-tech feel; instead, it means achieving clarity through functional precision rather than flashy animations that risk confusing or overwhelming local users. Trust in Japan is built on perceived stability and careful data handling, so you can maintain a modern, premium aesthetic while prioritizing extreme simplicity in text and reducing unnecessary clutter to empower users rather than condescend to them.",
